Looks fine, but I think it will fail in practice.
A voter that calls isGranted() doesn't get its own AccessDecision. Both decide() and isGranted() do `$accessDecision ??= end($this->accessDecisionStack)`, so the nested votes land in the same $votes.

A PasskeyVoter that exempts admins with $this->security->isGranted('ROLE_ADMIN') is enough: for a non-admin, the inner `RoleVoter` denial kills the re-authentication silently, and the tests miss it because createDenial() builds the votes by hand.

