by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-24T05:53:54Z

I reproduced it: 3 of the 4 combinations of outer and nested checks failed. The tests missed it for the reason you give.

The flag now names the attribute that a re-authentication can grant: `$vote->extraData[AuthenticatedVoter::RE_AUTHENTICATION] = $attribute`. The firewall starts a re-authentication only when a denying vote names the denied attribute. Like `supportsAttribute()`, this only looks at the denied attribute. But the voter still decides: a `CAN_DELETE_ACCOUNT` voter can re-authenticate the owner and deny everyone else with a 403. A list on the entry point cannot do that, because it only knows the name of the attribute.

